Spec: Itinerary
Platform: TypeScript

# Open this file in Zed to try the extension.
Purpose:
  Keep a trip itinerary organised by day.

Structure:
  ./src/itinerary.ts: itinerary implementation

Can modify:
  ./src/**
  ./test/*.ts

Depends on:
  @TripStorage

Must:
  Call @Itinerary.addPlace before returning.
  Use `TripStorage` to save changes.
  Validate the place name before saving
    and before updating trip days.

Must not:
  Purchase bookings or tickets.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Define the itinerary contract.
  [ ] #2 Implement input validation.
  [X] Add a storage interface.
  [!] Wait for storage availability.
  [?] Decide how to handle duplicate places.
  [-] Add booking integration.

Done when:
  Invalid input is rejected and valid changes are saved.

Scenario: missing place name
  Given the place name is empty
  When the person adds a place
  Then validation fails
  And no itinerary item is stored
  But existing items remain available

Example: validation result
  input place name: empty
  result error: missing place name
